.TH GLAZE 1 "2026-11-11" "Glaze 0.1.0" "Glaze User Commands"
.SH NAME
glaze \- inspect and drive the Glaze desktop service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B glaze
.IR command
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B glaze config get
.RI [ key ]
.br
.B glaze config set
.I key value
.br
.B glaze
.BR \-h | \-\-help | \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B glaze
is the command-line client for Glaze. It discovers the machine's real XDG
applications, runs the same deterministic search ranking as the shell, builds
and spawns launch commands through the safe argv path, reads and writes the
versioned user configuration, and can send a raw request to a running
.BR glaze-service
over the local control socket.
.PP
Run
.B glaze
with no arguments to print usage. Any failure prints a clear
.B glaze:
message to standard error and sets the exit code (see EXIT STATUS); the command
does not panic on bad input.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B apps
List the applications discovered from the XDG data directories, as a table.
Prints
.B "no applications discovered"
when the registry is genuinely empty.
.TP
.BI search " query " [ \-\-limit " N" ]
Search the registry and print ranked hits with their scores. The ranking is
deterministic: exact name match, then prefix, word-prefix, substring and
subsequence, with smaller contributions from keywords, generic name, comment and
desktop id. The default limit is 20; a limit of 0 requests the default. The
.B \-\-limit
flag accepts both
.B \-\-limit N
and
.BR \-\-limit=N .
.TP
.BI launch " id"
Look up the application by desktop id, print the resolved
.B argv
as JSON, and spawn it detached. Launching never involves a shell; the entry's
.B Exec
is tokenised and field codes are expanded.
.TP
.BI exec-line " id"
Print the exact launch argv for the application as pretty-printed JSON, without
spawning anything. Useful for auditing what
.B launch
will run.
.TP
.B status
Print the product name and version, the IPC protocol version, the number of
discovered applications, the configured theme and scheme, the configuration
file path, the control-socket path, and whether the socket currently exists.
.TP
.BR "config get" " [" key ]
With no key, print the whole effective configuration as TOML (defaults
included). With a key, print only that value. The configuration file path is
printed to standard error in both cases. See CONFIG KEYS for the accepted keys.
.TP
.BR "config set" " " key " " value
Validate the value for the key, update the configuration and write it back to
the TOML file, creating parent directories as needed. Prints the resulting
.B "key = value"
pair and the path that was written.
.TP
.BI ipc " request-json"
Send a single raw request, given as JSON on the command line, to a running
.BR glaze-service
over the control socket, and print the pretty-printed JSON response. This
command is available on Unix only; on other platforms it reports that the
control socket is Unix-only. The request JSON uses the Glaze IPC wire format,
for example
.BR '{"kind":"ping"}' .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help ", " help
Print usage and exit successfully.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version ", " version
Print
.B "Glaze Desktop <version>"
and exit.
.SH CONFIG KEYS
Accepted by
.B config get
and
.BR "config set" :
.TP
.B appearance.theme
.BR clay " or " classic .
.TP
.B appearance.scheme
.BR light " or " dark .
.TP
.B appearance.reduced_motion
A boolean:
.BR true/false ", " yes/no ", " on/off
or
.BR 1/0 .
.TP
.B panel.position
.BR top ", " bottom ", " left " or " right .
.TP
.B panel.height
An integer panel thickness in logical pixels, between 16 and 512 (inclusive).
.TP
.B panel.clock_24h
A boolean.
.TP
.B panel.show_seconds
A boolean.
.TP
.B launcher.pinned
A comma- or semicolon-separated list of desktop ids. An empty value clears the
pin list.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Location of
.BR glaze/config.toml ,
read and written by the
.B config
commands and reported by
.BR status .
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME ", " XDG_DATA_DIRS
Application-directory search path used by
.BR apps ", " search ", " launch " and " exec-line .
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Base directory for the control socket used by
.BR ipc .
.TP
.B XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP ", " LANG
Used for registry visibility rules and localised application names.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success. Also used for
.B \-\-help
and when no command is given.
.TP
.B 1
User error: an unknown command or flag, a missing or invalid argument or config
value, an unknown application id, or a failed IPC request.
.TP
.B 2
Internal error: configuration I/O, serialisation or IPC transport failure.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
glaze apps
glaze search firefox --limit 5
glaze exec-line org.mozilla.firefox
glaze launch org.mozilla.firefox
glaze config set appearance.scheme dark
glaze config get panel.position
glaze status
glaze ipc '{"kind":"ping"}'
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR glaze-session (1),
.BR glaze-service (1),
.BR glaze-shell (1),
.BR glaze-settings (1),
.BR glaze-compositor (1)
